    "packageDtsBytes": 550912,
    "_packageDtsBytesWhy": "Raised to 550 912 B (538 KB) by design/12 §4 F1 (2026-08-29): 549 122 B measured, +11 579 B, same ceil-to-1 KB rule. All of it is `07` §6.1/§6.2's builder-level option methods — `.signal()` / `.timeout()` / `.outsideTransaction()` / `.withExecMode()` on `Query`, `GroupedQuery`, `SetQuery`, `InsertQuery`, `UpdateQuery`, `DeleteQuery` and `PreparedQuery`, 28 signatures with their JSDoc, plus `QueryRunOptions` and the `run` field on five builder state records. They are written out per interface rather than behind one `QueryOptionMethods<Self>` mixin precisely so the TYPE numbers do not move, and they did not: the headline instantiation counts are unchanged on both compilers (82 028 / 133 822), every per-query fixture is unchanged, and the largest movement anywhere in the report is +0.75 % on a schema-declaration arm (55 705 -> 56 124 on TS 7). This is a size gate, not a type-performance one. Previously: raised to 537 600 B (525 KB) after design/12 §4 P merged (2026-08-29): the statement-path gate and the encode-path rewrite added 1 219 B of declarations (537 543 B measured), same rule. Previously: raised to 536 576 B (524 KB) after design/12 §4 D merged (2026-08-29): the docs-found `valuesMany` guard fix and the pg-like seam declarations added 1 758 B (536 324 B measured), same ceil-to-1 KB rule. Previously: raised to 534 528 B (522 KB) at the design/12 round-A integration (2026-08-29): the merged tree measures 533 563 B, which is S's 504 595 B plus B's builder-gap declarations (query/types.d.ts 54 843 -> 72 190 B across B and S together: `$all`, the six join signatures and two laterals, `withRecursive`/`fromRaw`, relation `avg`/`min`/`max`, and 07 §1.3's four handle interfaces) plus K4's schema DSL (`pgDomain`/`pgSequence`/`pgExtension`, the index item options, `partitionBy`/`partitionOf`, `clusterOn`, `t.raw`). Each branch had passed its own raised number; the SUM is what ships, so the budget is set at the merged measurement by the same ceil-to-1 KB rule and ratchets from here. Previous step: raised from 409 600 to 524 288 B by design/12 §3 S, the session layer, measured 377 261 B before and 504 595 B after (design/07 §4.2's ~50 error classes, §1.3's handle interfaces, the src/session, src/observe and src/pooler declaration files). This is a SIZE gate and not a type-performance one: the headline instantiation counts moved +1.9 % over the whole round (80 485 -> 82 028 on TS 5.9.3), inside design/12 §3 B's +2 % band. tools/budgets.json gates the same bytes at 900 KB against design/08 §1.2 and passes; this number is the tighter of the two and still ratchets.",
